NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/config.Config#FirstTurnRelevancePush kind=field
  digest=b3:906b900d6a23dc780ac5df558937143b782dcc4dd951a2f7d11deb0c00d0e308 file=neo/internal/config/config.go range=79:87 lang=go exported=true byte_range=4342:5003
  sig=bool
  doc=FirstTurnRelevancePush injects a bounded RELEVANCE retrieval into the\nactivation window on the FIRST turn of a conversation only. Neocortex.Activate's\npushed tiers (Pinned/Timeline/Recent) are recency-based and query-INDEPENDENT\n(activate.go: the query arg is unused), so on the opening message the agent\ncarries recency but NOT relevance-to-the-ask unless it reactively calls\nmemory_recall. With this on, Neo runs pager.Retrieve(query) once on turn 1\nand injects the hits, so the opening turn has relevance-matched memory with\nno reactive tool call. After turn 1 the pull-not-push philosophy resumes.
EDGES
  ^contains=matrix/neo/internal/config.Config

